Cascade Types in JPA :
Cascade is a feature in JPA that automatically applies operations performed on a parent entity to its related child entities.
--> Instead of saving or deleting the parent and child separately, JPA can do it automatically.

Syntax :
@OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL)
private List<Employee> employees;
Here,
cascade = CascadeType.ALL
means : Apply all operations (save, update, delete, etc.) from the parent to the child.

Types of Cascade :
| Cascade Type | Purpose                               | Example
| ------------ | ------------------------------------- |------------------------------------
| PERSIST      | Save child automatically              |@OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.PERSIST)
|              |                                       |private List<Employee> employees;
|              |                                       |
| MERGE        | Update child automatically            |department.setName("Software");
|              |                                       |emp.setName("David");
|              |                                       |departmentRepository.save(department);
|              |                                       |
| REMOVE       | Delete child automatically            |departmentRepository.delete(department);
|              |                                       |
| REFRESH      | Reload child from database            |entityManager.refresh(department);
|              |                                       |
| DETACH       | Detach child from persistence context |entityManager.detach(department);
|              |                                       |
| ALL          | Apply all cascade operations          |@OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL)
|              |                                       |private List<Employee> employees;
