Pagination and Sorting in Spring Data JPA

Pagination is the process of dividing a large number of records into smaller pages instead of loading all records at once.
Simple Definition : 
Instead of showing 10,000 records, show:
Page 1 → 10 records
Page 2 → 10 records
Page 3 → 10 records
--> This improves application performance and user experience.

Sorting is the process of arranging records in ascending or descending order based on one or more fields.
Example:
Salary (Highest → Lowest)
Name (A → Z)
Date (Newest → Oldest)

Pagination Syntax :
Spring Data JPA provides the Pageable interface.

Repository:
public interface EmployeeRepository
extends JpaRepository<Employee, Long> {}

Service:
Pageable pageable = PageRequest.of(0, 5);
Page<Employee> page = employeeRepository.findAll(pageable);
explanation :
PageRequest.of(0,5)
0 → First page (page numbering starts from 0)
5 → Number of records per page
