Auditing is a JPA feature used to automatically track who created or modified an entity and when those actions occurred.
--> Auditing automatically stores information such as:
1. Who created the record?
2. When was it created?
3. Who updated it?
4. When was it updated?

Auditing Annotations :
| Annotation           | Purpose                                                        |
| -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------|
| `@CreatedDate`       | Stores creation date                                           |
| `@LastModifiedDate`  | Stores last update date                                        |
| `@CreatedBy`         | Stores creator name                                            |
| `@LastModifiedBy`    | Stores last modifier name                                      |
| `@EnableJpaAuditing` | Enables auditing                                               |
| `@EntityListeners`   | Tells JPA to listen for entity events such as insert and update|

to Enable Auditing
Create a configuration class.
@Configuration
@EnableJpaAuditing
public class AuditConfig {}
