A Transaction is a sequence of one or more database operations that are treated as a single unit of work.
A transaction follows the rule:
1. Either all operations succeed, or all operations fail.
2. This is called Atomicity.

@Transactional is a Spring annotation that ensures all database operations 
inside a method are executed within a single transaction.
If one operation fails, all previous operations are rolled back.

--> Commit permanently saves all changes made during a transaction to the database.
--> Rollback cancels all changes made during a transaction and restores the database to its previous state.

ACID Properties : Every transaction follows ACID.
A – Atomicity
Definition:
All operations succeed or all fail.

C – Consistency
Definition:
A transaction moves the database from one valid state to another valid state.

I – Isolation
Definition:
Multiple transactions should not interfere with each other.

D – Durability
Definition:
Once a transaction is committed, the data is permanently stored even if the system crashes.

